{"command":"node -e \"\n// 4194304 = 0x400000\n// This is a typical base address for x86-64 Linux executables\n\n// Let's see what the first 32-bit value at file offset 0 would be at address 0x400000\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst buf = fs.readFileSync('/app/a.out');\n\n// If we add 0x400000 to file offsets, we get:\n// File offset 0 -> Virtual address 0x400000\n// File offset 4 -> Virtual address 0x400004\n// etc.\n\nconst base = 0x400000;\nconsole.log('First few values with base 0x400000:');\nfor (let i = 0; i < 64; i += 4) {\n    const val = buf.readUInt32LE(i);\n    const addr = base + i;\n    console.log('Address ' + addr + ': ' + val);\n}\n\""}